        "parms": "# ~bp and ~vcf — bands and resonant sweeps\nA ~bp passes a band around a centre frequency. Q sets its width: higher is narrower, 1 by default. Since libYSE 3.1 the centre passes at full level whatever the Q. A ~vcf is a resonant bandpass whose centre is a signal, so it can sweep at audio rate; sharpness sets how narrow it is.\nMax's vcf~ is a similar filter, with a resonance argument. Here a sharpness of 0 turns the filtering off and passes the input through, and ~vcf stays silent until both of its signal inlets are connected.",
        "type": ".text"
